@*
    Connectivity indicator for data-entry screens.

    On a range with patchy cellular, a failed save shows up as one "Ett fel uppstod" per attempt and
    nothing tells the operator that the PROBLEM is the network rather than the data. This badge makes
    the state standing rather than per-attempt: green while saves land, red — with the words —
    the moment one does not.

    Wiring: call `hpskSetConnection(ok)` after every server round trip on the screen. Every badge on
    the page updates, so a screen that renders one in a header and one near a save button stays
    consistent.

        try { const r = await fetch(...); hpskSetConnection(r.ok); }
        catch (e) { hpskSetConnection(false); }

    ⚠️ Report the FETCH outcome, not `navigator.onLine`. A phone associated with a range AP that has
    no upstream reports onLine = true, which is exactly the situation this badge exists to expose.

    It starts neutral (grey) and NEVER guesses: until a real request has been made, "we don't know"
    is the honest state — a green badge before the first save is a promise nothing has kept.
*@
<span class="badge bg-secondary hpsk-conn-badge" title="Nätverksstatus"><i class="bi bi-wifi"></i></span>
@if (ViewData["hpskConnBadgeScriptRendered"] == null)
{
    ViewData["hpskConnBadgeScriptRendered"] = true;
    <script>
    // Guarded so several badges on one page define the function once.
    if (!window.hpskSetConnection) {
        window.hpskSetConnection = function (ok) {
            document.querySelectorAll('.hpsk-conn-badge').forEach(function (el) {
                if (ok) {
                    el.className = 'badge bg-success hpsk-conn-badge';
                    el.innerHTML = '<i class="bi bi-wifi"></i>';
                    el.title = 'Uppkopplad';
                } else {
                    el.className = 'badge bg-danger hpsk-conn-badge';
                    el.innerHTML = '<i class="bi bi-wifi-off"></i> Ingen kontakt';
                    el.title = 'Ingen kontakt med servern — åtgärder sparas inte';
                }
            });
        };
    }
    </script>
}
